# FBE.2b — synth pipeline preserves framework/ prefix on shipped paths

2026-05-03. v0.1.0 reviewer foldback closes the doc-vs-synth
path-shape divergence (HIGH 1) by fixing the synth pipeline to
preserve canonical's `framework/<comp>/` shape rather than
stripping the `framework/` prefix on shipped paths. Reviewer
dossier:
`<workspace>/.scratch/claude-output/loam-user-review-2026-05-03.md`.
Parent plan:
`docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion.md` §3
Decision D + §4 (FBE.2b inserted).
Sub-plan:
`docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion-fbe2b.md`.

Decision D from the parent plan locked: fix the synth, not the
docs. 15+ doc files reference `framework/<comp>/` paths
consistently; rewriting them all would be a 50+ edit sweep with
high risk. The synth strip is a targeted edit in
`synth.py:_build_synthetic_tree` (lines 302-312 pre-FBE.2b).
FBE.2b removes the strip + updates docstrings + flips the three
in-fence test files that asserted on post-strip paths.

Establishes `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/` as a
NEW sealed component (sidecar + invariant), mirroring FBE.2's
loam-cli pattern. Pre-FBE.2b, the manifest-owner component rode
universal-paths admission alone (verified at FBE.2 + FBE.5 — no
`tests/SEAL_COMMIT` or `test_no_sealed_amendments.py`); FBE.2b is
a substantive code edit so the universal-paths-only ride is no
longer enough.

Structural delta (within fence + universal admissions):

  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/src/loam/publish_framework_only/synth.py`
    — drop the framework/ prefix strip (~10 lines); update
    module docstring + _LeafEntry.synthetic_path docstring +
    _build_synthetic_tree docstring + adjacent comment to
    describe prefix-preserving behaviour; preserve
    saw_framework_leaf semantic (just no longer coupled to the
    strip).
  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/src/loam/publish_framework_only/cli.py`
    — drop the obsolete "framework/framework/<comp>/ doubling"
    rationale from --help description; replace with the
    prefix-preserving description.
  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/tests/test_AC_SFR_2_synthesis_pipeline.py`
    — flip path-shape assertions to prefix-preserved paths;
    invert the no-doubled-framework-prefix assertion to
    no-doubled-framework/framework + at-least-one-framework/
    positive shape check; HC#4 byte-content pairs become
    same-path pairs for framework leaves.
  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/tests/test_AC_OSS_3_synthesis_drops_dev_only.py`
    — flip ships-paths + drops-paths + audit-excludes-paths
    assertions to prefix-preserved paths.
  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/tests/test_AC_OSS_M9_substitution_after_partition.py`
    — flip tree-entry path assertions to prefix-preserved paths.
  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/tests/SEAL_COMMIT`
    — NEW sidecar (placeholder HEAD; bumped to BASELINE at
    apply, then to seal SHA at seal).
  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/tests/test_no_sealed_amendments.py`
    — NEW structural fence test (AC.FBE.2b.S; mirrors FBE.2's
    loam-cli shape; allowed_prefixes includes
    `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/` + standard
    cross-component admissions per FBE.2 precedent).

AC surface (per sub-plan §4):

  - AC.FBE.2b.1 — synth.py drops the prefix-strip rewrite.
  - AC.FBE.2b.2 — synth.py docstrings updated to describe
    prefix-preserving behaviour.
  - AC.FBE.2b.3 — cli.py --help description rationale
    rephrased.
  - AC.FBE.2b.4 — synth re-run produces framework/-prefixed
    paths in framework-only tree.
  - AC.FBE.2b.5/6/7 — three in-fence test files updated to
    assert on prefix-preserved paths and pass.
  - AC.FBE.2b.8 — eight other in-fence test files continue to
    pass byte-identically.
  - AC.FBE.2b.9 — NEW sidecar files exist; fence-test passes
    for FBE.2b BASELINE.
  - AC.FBE.2b.10 — partition.py / substitution.py /
    publish-mode-manifest.yaml unchanged; no other components
