    docs/rebuild/plans/.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - saw_framework_leaf semantic preserved as inline check
    (`source_path.startswith(f"{FRAMEWORK_PREFIX}/")`) rather
    than restructuring the loop — minimal-diff principle.
  - Sidecar shape mirrors FBE.2's loam-cli exactly (REPO_ROOT
    depth 5 — same parent.parent.parent.parent.parent
    traversal; same _seal_commit() helper; same allowed_prefixes
    admission shape with cross-component admissions for the
    FBE.5-fence-fifteen sweep + plugins/dev-sdlc/ + tools/loam/
    partner prefixes).
  - The bare-`framework` safety branch (currently elif clause)
    dropped entirely — it was vestigial (`ls-tree -r` never
    emits a leaf named exactly `framework`).
  - cli.py description preserves the manifest-path default
    clause and the pos-new-workspace --from clause; only the
    promotion / doubling rationale text changes.

Out of scope (per sub-plan §8):

  - Partition manifest content edits (no reclassification —
    path-shaping only).
  - Edits to partition.py or substitution.py.
  - Other components' descriptions / sources / tests / sidecars.
  - README / getting-started rewrites (already use
    framework/<comp>/ — FBE.2b aligns synth with these docs).
  - Re-staging the synth to a remote (FBE.6's job).
  - Pyproject metadata edits to any component.

BASELINE filled by loam amend apply (the pre-apply tip after
plan-doc + source-edit + manifest commits land). The
pos-publish-framework-only anchor's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar lands
at the seal SHA via `loam amend seal`.
